<%#
  The design shows a best-time-to-post panel with specific windows per platform,
  described as "based on your audience activity". That is a measurement of
  published performance, and none exists until a real account has posted
  history. Showing invented windows here would be exactly the fabricated
  performance claim the specification forbids (spec 22, 27), so the panel says
  what it needs instead.
%>
<% accounts = workspace.social_accounts.connected %>
<% simulated = accounts.any? && accounts.all?(&:mocked?) %>

<section class="rounded-card border border-border bg-blue-soft p-5">
  <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-normal">Best time to post</h2>

  <% if accounts.empty? %>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body">
      Prachar works this out from when your own audience actually engages.
      Connect an account and it will appear here once there is enough history.
    </p>
    <%= link_to "Connect an account",
          workspace_onboarding_connections_path(workspace_slug: workspace.slug),
          class: "mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center rounded-control bg-primary px-4 text-sm font-medium text-primary-contrast hover:bg-primary-hover" %>
  <% elsif simulated %>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body">
      Your connected accounts are simulated, so there is no real posting history to read.
      This fills in once a live account has published for a while.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body">
      Not enough published history yet to identify your best times.
      Keep posting and this will fill in.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</section>
